fix(view): persistent iframe was never taken out of its hidden parking node

v0.3.1 created the keep-alive iframe inside a display:none parking
container and then only mutated the FRAME's inline styles - the node itself
stayed inside the hidden parent, so the embedded page never appeared
(reload button had no effect either; the open-in-new-window tab worked
because it bypassed the frame).

- ensurePersistentFrame now attaches the iframe DIRECTLY to <body>
  (initially hidden). After creation the node is never re-parented - DOM
  moves would reload the iframe, defeating keep-alive. Show/hide is purely
  inline styles.
- z-index raised 5 -> 99999: the frame lives in the root stacking context
  and mid-range shell containers painted over it; it only ever covers the
  stage rectangle.
- scroll listener (capture) added so the fixed geometry follows any
  scrollable ancestor.
- diagnostics: <html data-dsh-frame="visible WxH@x,y | hidden:reason"> for
  field verification in the Elements panel.
- version 0.3.2.
